-- D-33: FSQM-035 draft revised to the owner's answers of 2026-09-22 (still DRAFT).
--
-- The draft said the dry storage room is fully dry with no sink in or next to it. It is not: the
-- 3-compartment sink is inside the room, by the exit and at least 20 feet from any stored material.
-- Chemicals are currently kept near that sink, unlocked, until the FSQM-032 locker is bought, and the
-- locker may then stand in the dry storage room (11.6.4.2 does not require a separate room). The room
-- is swept monthly, not weekly. There is ample room to clean behind the shelving (33.7).
--
-- Procedure goes from 29 to 31 lines: the sink rule and the interim chemical shelf are new lines.

begin;

do $guard$
begin
  if (select count(*) from public.sop_documents where sop_number = 'FSQM-035' and status = 'draft') <> 1 then
    raise exception 'FSQM-035 is not a single draft.';
  end if;
  if (select jsonb_array_length(content->'procedure') from public.sop_documents where sop_number = 'FSQM-035') <> 29
     or not (select content->'procedure' ->> 1 like '%no sink, floor drain%' from public.sop_documents where sop_number = 'FSQM-035') then
    raise exception 'FSQM-035 procedure is not the 2026-09-22 draft this migration revises.';
  end if;
end $guard$;

update public.sop_documents
   set content = content || jsonb_build_object(
         'procedure', $p$["Where things are kept", "• Dry storage room: dry ingredients, packaging and finished product, each on its own shelving, all kept dry.", "• The room's only wet area is the 3-compartment sink, by the exit and at least 20 feet from any stored material. No ingredients, packaging or finished product are stored or staged near the sink, and water spilled outside the sink is mopped up at once (SQF 11.6.3.1).", "• Walk-in refrigerator: chilled ingredients, and in-process or finished product held cold. Walk-in freezer: anything that needs to stay frozen. Both are monitored under SOP-401.", "• Chemicals are kept only in the locked chemical locker under FSQM-032, never on the ingredient, packaging or finished-product shelving and never in the walk-ins. The locker may stand in the dry storage room: on its own at floor level with a spill tray inside, never above or beside ingredient, allergen or packaging shelving, and with nothing stored on or against it (SQF 11.6.4.2).", "• Until the locker is installed, chemicals are kept on their own shelf beside the 3-compartment sink, away from all stored material. This is a known gap, recorded in FSQM-032.", "• No overflow or temporary storage is used. Everything fits in the rooms above (SQF 11.6.1.5, 11.6.1.6). Before any other place is used, the SQF Practitioner assesses the risk in writing and this program is revised to include it.", "Receipt", "• Every delivery is checked and recorded on FRM-301 under SOP-2.3.4: supplier approved, packaging intact, lot and best-by recorded, and the temperature of chilled goods.", "• Chilled goods are received at 41°F or below and go into the walk-in first, before anything else is put away. Frozen goods are received frozen.", "• Dry goods and packaging are put away the same day. Until then they wait in the receiving area, off the floor, away from production and never on the production floor.", "• A delivery that fails its check is held on FRM-702 under FSQM-018 and kept apart from accepted stock.", "Keeping things apart", "• Ingredients, packaging and finished product each have their own shelving in the dry storage room.", "• Allergen ingredients are kept on their own shelf, labelled, and never above non-allergen ingredients (SQF 11.6.1.2, 2.8.1.3).", "• In the walk-in, in-process and finished product is covered and kept on shelves above raw chilled ingredients such as eggs and dairy, never below them (SQF 11.6.1.2).", "• Held or rejected stock is tagged under FSQM-018 and kept apart from stock in use.", "• Clean utensils and spare equipment parts are kept covered and off the floor, never in the chemical locker.", "Shelving and pallets", "• All stock is kept off the floor, on shelving or on clean, dry, undamaged pallets, with a gap from the walls wide enough to clean and inspect behind (SQF 11.6.3.2).", "• Shelving is metal, wire or plastic - smooth and cleanable. Wooden shelving is not used.", "• The dry storage room floor is swept monthly, including under the shelving and pallets, and any spill is cleaned up when it happens (SQF 11.6.3.2).", "Stock rotation", "• Stock is used FEFO: the soonest best-by first. New deliveries are put behind or below older stock of the same item (SQF 11.6.1.3).", "• Rotation is checked monthly on the GMP inspection, FRM-913, row 11.6.1.", "Shelf life", "• Materials: the best-by date is recorded on FRM-301 at receipt, and checked when the material is taken for weighing. Expired material is not used; it is held on FRM-702 (SQF 11.6.1.4).", "• Opened ingredients are closed again after use, or moved into a lidded container labelled with the product name, lot and best-by, so they keep their shelf life and their traceability.", "• In-process product: batter is all baked the day it is mixed. Anything else held for later is covered, labelled with what it is, the lot and the date it was made, and kept in the walk-in. Anything unlabelled is discarded.", "• Rework: the only rework is re-pouching a pouch that fails its seal. Re-pouched product keeps its original lot and best-by (FSQM-018).", "• Finished product: its shelf life is set on FRM-704 and its best-by and lot are printed on every pack. Finished product is dispatched FEFO under FSQM-036."]$p$::jsonb,
         'revision_history', $r$"New - 2026-09-22 - DRAFT under D-33, for the eight Non-Compliant findings against 11.6.1 and 11.6.3.\n\nWHAT THE SITE DOES NOW (owner, 2026-09-22): one dry storage room holds ingredients, packaging and finished product on separate shelving; stock is on a mix of shelving and pallets; the oldest is used first; allergen ingredients have their own labelled shelf; the 3-compartment sink is inside the dry storage room, by the exit and at least 20 feet from any stored material; chemicals are kept unlocked near the sink until a locker is bought, and the locker may then stand in the dry storage room; the room is swept monthly; there is ample room to clean behind and under the shelving and pallets; the walk-ins hold chilled ingredients and in-process or finished product; no overflow storage is used; deliveries are sometimes put straight away and sometimes staged first.\n\nONE DOCUMENT, NO NEW FORM: the workbook allowed for an SOP-4xx as well. Receiving is already recorded on FRM-301 and storage is already checked monthly on FRM-913, so a second document and a new form would record the same things twice.\n\nTHE SINK AND 11.6.3.1: the code asks for dry storage to be located away from wet areas. The room is not wholly dry; the site's control is distance (the sink is by the exit, at least 20 feet from stored material), no stock stored or staged near it, and spilled water mopped up at once. An auditor may still raise it; moving the sink or storage is the only complete answer.\n\nCHEMICAL LOCKER: 11.6.4.2 does not require a separate room. The locker may stand in the dry storage room if it is locked, signed, ventilated, at floor level with a spill tray, and apart from ingredient, allergen and packaging shelving. It is not yet bought (see FSQM-032).\n\nSWEEPING: monthly, as the site does now (11.6.3.2 asks only for a pre-determined frequency). Monthly is thin for a room with flour in it, because flour dust draws pests; weekly would be easier to defend."$r$::jsonb)
 where sop_number = 'FSQM-035' and status = 'draft';

do $verify$
declare c jsonb := (select content from public.sop_documents where sop_number = 'FSQM-035');
begin
  if jsonb_array_length(c->'procedure') <> 31 then raise exception 'FSQM-035 procedure not 31 lines.'; end if;
  if c::text like '%no sink, floor drain%' or c::text like '%swept weekly%' or c::text like '%TO CONFIRM BEFORE ISSUE%' then
    raise exception 'FSQM-035 still carries superseded wording.';
  end if;
end $verify$;

commit;
